WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:30.000
{IF YOU ARE SEEING THIS, YOUR PLAYER IS NOT RENDERING THE SUBTITLES PROPERLY. PLEASE REFER TO http://saizen-fansubs.com/?section=playback FOR THE INTENDED PLAYBACK.}

00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:24.600
The game is over!

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:27.850
Kaido High School wins both the spring and summer seasons!

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:31.130
Are you here, Mom?

00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:35.180
Dammit.

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:40.030
Hello?

00:00:40.030 --> 00:00:41.150
Hey, Shigeno.

00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:43.730
Are you quietly staying home?

00:00:43.730 --> 00:00:45.950
Oh, it's you, Tashiro.

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:48.250
Sorry it's me.

00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:50.330
And what do you want?

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:53.010
Kaido won.

00:00:53.630 --> 00:00:59.260
It looks like we were the only ones in the preliminary round that troubled them.

00:01:01.070 --> 00:01:02.180
Yeah...

00:01:03.140 --> 00:01:06.630
By the way, I suppose you haven't been out that much with that foot of yours, right?

00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:07.590
Huh?

00:01:15.770 --> 00:01:17.130
I was wondering what you were going on about.

00:01:17.130 --> 00:01:19.560
It's just the local summer festival.

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:23.500
I didn't want to go to crowded places in the middle of summer.

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:25.110
Well, don't say that.

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:26.550
That's right. That's right.

00:01:26.550 --> 00:01:28.640
We need to stretch our wings once in a while.

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:30.720
You stretch them too often.

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:32.080
Oh, there they are.

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:34.730
Hey! Over here! Over here!

00:01:34.730 --> 00:01:37.210
We have beautiful girls here too, sir!

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:41.190
Hi!

00:01:41.190 --> 00:01:42.050
Yo!

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:44.010
Where?

00:01:44.010 --> 00:01:45.130
Hey!

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:50.800
Hey,

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:53.930
have you guys started studying for the entrance exams?

00:01:53.930 --> 00:01:55.640
Well, slowly.

00:01:56.130 --> 00:01:59.430
<i>I should have gone for the employment applications.</i>

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:01.900
By the way, Miyazaki,

00:02:02.510 --> 00:02:04.110
you're aiming for a state university, right?

00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:05.820
Yeah.

00:02:06.190 --> 00:02:09.010
Your studies must be hard then.

00:02:09.010 --> 00:02:10.300
Well, yeah.

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:13.990
But compared to baseball training, it's nothing.

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:16.200
You may be right about that.

00:02:17.090 --> 00:02:19.170
The baseball club, huh?

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:43.940
Kaido won.

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:48.400
We went against that Kaido, right?

00:02:49.250 --> 00:02:51.870
It kind of feels like a dream.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.370
I never would've imagined it a year ago.

00:02:56.830 --> 00:02:57.910
No.

00:02:57.910 --> 00:03:00.540
If we hadn't met Shigeno, even now...

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:11.220
So this is where you were.

00:03:11.630 --> 00:03:14.020
The crowd was getting to me.

00:03:14.680 --> 00:03:17.220
Don't mind me and carry on playing.

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:26.980
I feel sorry for you so I'll stay.

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:35.280
Shimizu...

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:36.530
Yes?

00:03:36.530 --> 00:03:38.930
What are you going to do after you graduate?

00:03:38.930 --> 00:03:40.220
Oh...

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:42.960
I'm thinking of going to university for now.

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:45.390
In a four-year program if possible.

00:03:45.390 --> 00:03:46.980
Oh right.

00:03:46.980 --> 00:03:49.870
You're smart even though you don't look like it.

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:50.750
Hey!

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:52.680
And what are you going to do, Honda?

00:03:53.160 --> 00:03:57.000
It's going to be hard getting considered for a professional team with your foot injured, right?

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:58.320
Yeah.

00:03:58.320 --> 00:04:01.940
My dad even said he'd introduce me to a university.

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:04.550
In that case, maybe we could be together-

00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:05.800
But I refused it.

00:04:06.650 --> 00:04:10.610
I may not be able to join this year,
but I may be able to do something next year.

00:04:10.610 --> 00:04:15.490
Once my foot is healed, I just need to get a tryout for a professional team somewhere and pass.

00:04:22.050 --> 00:04:23.460
I see.

00:04:38.430 --> 00:04:43.310
Once we graduate, we won't be able to see each other that easily then.

00:04:43.310 --> 00:04:44.720
What?

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:46.530
Did you say something?

00:04:46.530 --> 00:04:47.980
It's nothing.

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:55.700
I just said that when you become a pro,
I'd be the first one to get your autograph; that's all.

00:05:00.590 --> 00:05:01.550
Yeah.

00:05:06.550 --> 00:05:07.880
What!?

00:05:07.880 --> 00:05:09.330
Are you sure, Dad?

00:05:09.720 --> 00:05:10.380
Yeah.

00:05:10.380 --> 00:05:12.430
I just heard from Katsuragi.

00:05:12.430 --> 00:05:15.350
After seeing that game against Kaido, he must have changed the upper management's evaluation.

00:05:15.780 --> 00:05:18.700
They judged that your injury will have healed before joining them.

00:05:19.690 --> 00:05:21.310
<i>No way!</i>

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:23.270
The Oceans!?

00:05:23.270 --> 00:05:27.150
When you say the Oceans, you mean the Yokohama Blue Oceans?

00:05:27.150 --> 00:05:28.530
Are you really joining the pros?

00:05:28.530 --> 00:05:30.330
Well, yeah.

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:32.650
For now, it looks like I'll be employed somewhere.

00:05:33.050 --> 00:05:39.120
<i>And I'll be able to wear the same uniform as both my dads. I can't ask for anything more.</i>

00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:41.240
So you're joining the pros.

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:45.160
Well, then there won't be any regrets if the baseball club breaks up.

00:05:45.160 --> 00:05:46.080
You're right.

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:47.080
Huh?

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:49.070
The baseball club is going to break up?

00:05:49.070 --> 00:05:49.670
What?

00:05:49.670 --> 00:05:51.050
You didn't hear about it?

00:05:51.530 --> 00:05:57.060
It's pretty much decided that the activities of the baseball club will be stopped once the third-years graduate.

00:05:57.060 --> 00:05:58.240
What!?

00:05:58.240 --> 00:06:01.800
There'll only be five members left so it can't be helped.

00:06:02.430 --> 00:06:03.640
Wait a second!

00:06:03.640 --> 00:06:07.630
There may be new students coming in next year!

00:06:07.630 --> 00:06:08.900
Why are they being stopped!?

00:06:09.220 --> 00:06:11.330
Even if you argue with us,

00:06:11.330 --> 00:06:15.400
their new captain, Taiga, seems to want out, so there's nothing we can do.

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:17.740
Taiga wants out!?

00:06:18.500 --> 00:06:19.410
What?

00:06:19.730 --> 00:06:21.070
So you came to talk about that.

00:06:21.070 --> 00:06:22.400
What do you mean "What"!?

00:06:22.990 --> 00:06:25.880
What's the point if you, the best player, doesn't help pull it along?

00:06:25.880 --> 00:06:28.120
You may even have new members next year-

00:06:28.120 --> 00:06:29.830
I don't want to.

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:33.930
Why do I have to do something so bothersome?

00:06:33.930 --> 00:06:35.420
What!?

00:06:35.420 --> 00:06:40.200
Besides, wasn't the baseball club something you started in order to defeat Kaido?

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:45.140
And when you leave, is there any reason left to continue that club?

00:06:45.530 --> 00:06:47.120
You bastard.

00:06:47.120 --> 00:06:50.120
Are you still playing baseball because of advantages and disadvantages!?

00:06:52.340 --> 00:06:53.940
I'm disappointed in you, Taiga!

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:58.400
Even you were fighting with your utmost against Kaido!

00:06:58.400 --> 00:07:01.030
Was that motivation of yours a lie!?

00:07:01.030 --> 00:07:02.960
Taiga!

00:07:02.960 --> 00:07:06.330
I can't take responsibility like you, Senpai.

00:07:07.800 --> 00:07:10.460
What are you saying I can do?

00:07:10.930 --> 00:07:14.890
It's not like I can throw a gyroball like you.

00:07:14.890 --> 00:07:17.840
I'm not even a slugger that can score runs.

00:07:18.170 --> 00:07:22.810
I won't be able to show everyone the dream of going to Koshien.

00:07:25.390 --> 00:07:26.850
That's okay.

00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:32.900
There won't be any idiots unreasonably saying you should defeat Kaido anymore.

00:07:33.350 --> 00:07:39.050
Even if you lose in the first game, you guys should just make your own team.

00:07:39.880 --> 00:07:42.490
Just take it easy, new captain.

00:07:43.110 --> 00:07:44.170
See ya.

00:07:45.510 --> 00:07:47.740
<i>It's not okay to lose.</i>

00:07:48.170 --> 00:07:52.490
<i>After showing me that dream... that's just dirty!</i>

00:07:56.550 --> 00:07:57.920
I'm happy for you.

00:07:58.520 --> 00:08:01.760
Your cast is off now, and it looks as though you're progressing well.

00:08:01.760 --> 00:08:03.010
Yeah.

00:08:03.010 --> 00:08:06.180
Well, the rehabilitation is going to be hard after this.

00:08:06.920 --> 00:08:09.650
Just don't push yourself with an unreasonable pace, okay?

00:08:09.650 --> 00:08:10.890
I know.

00:08:11.470 --> 00:08:12.680
Hey, Mom,

00:08:12.680 --> 00:08:14.450
could you drop me around here?

00:08:22.090 --> 00:08:24.200
You have some talent there.

00:08:24.610 --> 00:08:26.660
You want to be a baseball player?

00:08:27.180 --> 00:08:28.320
Goro-kun!

00:08:30.120 --> 00:08:31.950
So your cast came off.

00:08:31.950 --> 00:08:32.890
Yeah.

00:08:32.890 --> 00:08:34.530
Just today.

00:08:34.530 --> 00:08:37.300
I'm glad you seem to be recovering well.

00:08:37.300 --> 00:08:43.050
I was thinking of contacting you, but right after Koshien I was playing abroad.

00:08:43.600 --> 00:08:45.630
Playing abroad?

00:08:45.630 --> 00:08:49.930
With Mayumura and Yakushiji,
we were selected for the all-star team.

00:08:50.510 --> 00:08:54.290
We had a friendly game against the American High School All-Star Team.

00:08:54.290 --> 00:08:55.320
Oh.

00:08:55.320 --> 00:08:56.900
And did you guys win?

00:08:57.490 --> 00:08:59.000
We won twice and lost twice.

00:08:59.000 --> 00:09:00.400
It was a draw.

00:09:01.090 --> 00:09:05.990
But, then again, they weren't playing with their best players like we were.

00:09:05.990 --> 00:09:10.390
Some of their players had started training for their pro teams and weren't playing.

00:09:11.010 --> 00:09:14.420
American baseball sure is limitless.

00:09:15.800 --> 00:09:16.450
By the way,

00:09:16.450 --> 00:09:17.920
what did you want?

00:09:18.620 --> 00:09:22.210
It's not like you came here just to see my face, did you?

00:09:23.640 --> 00:09:25.840
You're quick at catching stuff, as always.

00:09:25.840 --> 00:09:28.090
The thing is, there's something I wanted to ask you.

00:09:28.590 --> 00:09:30.100
Something you wanted to ask me?

00:09:30.830 --> 00:09:33.230
Are you going to the professionals?

00:09:37.670 --> 00:09:38.440
Yeah.

00:09:38.440 --> 00:09:39.350
I'm going.

00:09:40.070 --> 00:09:46.400
It's something I heard from a newspaper reporter,
but it looks as though the Warriors are going to draft me.

00:09:48.460 --> 00:09:49.900
I see.

00:09:49.900 --> 00:09:53.290
That means our match will continue on the professional field then.

00:09:54.760 --> 00:09:57.950
It looks as though the Oceans are going to draft me.

00:09:57.950 --> 00:10:00.260
It means we'll be enemies.

00:10:02.710 --> 00:10:04.730
Congratulations, Goro-kun!

00:10:04.730 --> 00:10:08.970
To be honest, I was worried that you might not be able to join the pros this year because of your injury.

00:10:09.450 --> 00:10:10.820
I'm so happy for you.

00:10:11.740 --> 00:10:15.310
I'm sure your dad in heaven is happy for you.

00:10:16.090 --> 00:10:17.170
Toshi.

00:10:18.500 --> 00:10:19.560
Yeah.

00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:22.520
I'm home!

00:10:23.140 --> 00:10:25.240
Aw, no one's home.

00:10:27.440 --> 00:10:29.400
Something to eat?

00:10:31.450 --> 00:10:33.300
Here's something.

00:10:31.990 --> 00:10:34.870
We have an announcement of a new record from America.

00:10:35.670 --> 00:10:42.250
Joe Gibson from the Major League Titans in New York
has just won his 300th game 3-2.

00:10:44.550 --> 00:10:47.760
Although he's now 41 years old, the speed of his fastball has not declined.

00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:50.930
Excluding the three years he played in Japan... {M: and I can't catch the rest because Goro starts talking}

00:10:50.930 --> 00:10:52.800
I didn't know...

00:10:52.800 --> 00:10:56.350
That old man is still playing!?

00:10:57.150 --> 00:11:01.620
I owe this achievement to the support from my family, friends, and teammates.

00:11:01.620 --> 00:11:08.490
But, above all things, my continued performance is owed to the inspiration I get from a young baseball player in Japan.

00:11:08.490 --> 00:11:09.540
Who, like me, 

00:11:09.540 --> 00:11:16.580
continues to play with great enthusiasm and the dream that someday we both can compete against each other on the same field.

00:11:18.540 --> 00:11:23.540
This is a free fansub.

00:11:18.540 --> 00:11:23.540
Not for sale or rent.

00:11:34.970 --> 00:11:36.680
<i>Sorry, boy.</i>

00:11:39.690 --> 00:11:41.860
<i>See you again, boy.</i>

00:12:00.640 --> 00:12:01.510
Hey.

00:12:01.510 --> 00:12:03.580
You've sure grown, Goro-kun.

00:12:05.290 --> 00:12:07.650
I'm sorry, Kusakabe-san.

00:12:07.650 --> 00:12:11.290
You're busy working as a translator for the Warriors, right?

00:12:11.290 --> 00:12:16.120
Well, my main work nowadays is to scout foreign players.

00:12:16.630 --> 00:12:19.850
I've been travelling back and forth between Japan and America throughout the year.

00:12:20.210 --> 00:12:21.700
Oh.

00:12:21.700 --> 00:12:23.550
But this sure brings back memories.

00:12:24.080 --> 00:12:26.320
The last time was when we went to Los Angeles together.

00:12:26.910 --> 00:12:30.070
Come to think of it, you got injured by that girl that came along-

00:12:30.070 --> 00:12:31.410
Kusakabe-san.

00:12:32.550 --> 00:12:34.600
T-That is...

00:12:34.600 --> 00:12:36.400
I was able to get in contact.

00:12:36.400 --> 00:12:39.100
This just came through by fax this morning.

00:12:39.100 --> 00:12:40.700
It's the reply from Gibson.

00:12:44.490 --> 00:12:46.290
To my dear Honda.

00:12:46.290 --> 00:12:47.060
No.

00:12:47.060 --> 00:12:48.420
Shigeno Goro-kun.

00:12:48.990 --> 00:12:54.790
I have been following your progress from time to time through my old friend Kusakabe.

00:12:56.200 --> 00:13:05.770
<i>And every time I receive news of your enthusiasm, it reminds me of your father, and I find myself overcome with emotion.</i>

00:13:06.170 --> 00:13:08.110
<i>Regarding my statement in the interview,</i>

00:13:08.110 --> 00:13:18.120
<i>I wanted to tell you that it was merely an expression of my gratitude for the inspiration you have given me.</i>

00:13:19.010 --> 00:13:25.460
<i>I know that it's difficult enough to live in a place with a different language and culture.</i>

00:13:26.390 --> 00:13:31.370
<i>But of course my dream is that one day you and I can meet again in the Majors.</i>

00:13:32.320 --> 00:13:34.010
<i>In a couple of years...</i>

00:13:34.510 --> 00:13:44.080
<i>I will wait and look forward to the day you come across the ocean after you have played a couple of years of Japanese baseball.</i>

00:13:49.170 --> 00:13:50.190
What do you think?

00:13:51.020 --> 00:13:52.800
Are you satisfied?

00:13:58.630 --> 00:13:59.690
Yeah.

00:14:00.500 --> 00:14:05.700
I'm satisfied and I've realized what I really want to do.

00:14:05.700 --> 00:14:08.170
All right! All right!

00:14:08.170 --> 00:14:09.500
Play!

00:14:09.500 --> 00:14:11.130
You can do it!

00:14:11.540 --> 00:14:12.550
Go!

00:14:15.410 --> 00:14:17.090
Yes. This is Katsuragi.

00:14:17.090 --> 00:14:18.150
It's me.

00:14:18.150 --> 00:14:19.470
Oh, Chief Yoneda.

00:14:20.080 --> 00:14:21.360
What is the matter?

00:14:21.360 --> 00:14:23.190
I have sad news.

00:14:23.190 --> 00:14:23.930
Yes?

00:14:23.930 --> 00:14:25.980
Shigeno Goro...  just refused our offer into the pros.

00:14:25.980 --> 00:14:28.170
Shigeno Goro...  just refused our offer into the pros.

00:14:28.170 --> 00:14:29.150
What!?

00:14:30.100 --> 00:14:33.230
You refused the offer into the pros and plan to go to America alone!?

00:14:33.960 --> 00:14:35.890
Are you seriously saying that!?

00:14:35.890 --> 00:14:36.730
Yeah.

00:14:37.180 --> 00:14:39.270
There's no point in you arguing against it.

00:14:39.270 --> 00:14:41.950
I've already decided.

00:14:45.980 --> 00:14:46.820
Hey.

00:14:46.820 --> 00:14:48.480
I'm not saying this as a bad thing.

00:14:48.480 --> 00:14:50.530
Think it over, Goro.

00:14:50.530 --> 00:14:56.140
You'll probably be able to get a contract in the Minors somewhere if you go for the tryouts.

00:14:56.800 --> 00:15:01.240
But it's a big mistake if you think you could rise up to the Majors with just a 150km/h pitch!

00:15:02.760 --> 00:15:05.990
Plus, you'll need to be able to speak the language and cook for yourself.

00:15:06.600 --> 00:15:09.550
It's best if you train here in Japan and improve your pitching-

00:15:08.570 --> 00:15:11.750
Dad, you're saying the same thing as Gibson.

00:15:11.750 --> 00:15:13.280
G-Gibson!?

00:15:14.470 --> 00:15:17.700
It's not like I'm looking lightly at Japanese baseball.

00:15:17.700 --> 00:15:22.600
It's just that if I did that, he'll retire by then!

00:15:22.600 --> 00:15:27.450
Dad's rival is waiting for me across the other side of the ocean!

00:15:33.990 --> 00:15:34.890
Do what you want!

00:15:41.200 --> 00:15:43.600
Of course Dad would get angry.

00:15:45.780 --> 00:15:47.180
Your father...

00:15:47.980 --> 00:15:57.150
asked the baseball team to give you his retired number if you should ever join the Oceans.

00:15:59.020 --> 00:16:01.000
But it's all right.

00:16:01.000 --> 00:16:03.730
I'll convince your father somehow.

00:16:03.730 --> 00:16:04.780
Because...

00:16:05.340 --> 00:16:10.790
You'll always be Honda Goro.

00:16:12.560 --> 00:16:13.500
You go.

00:16:14.250 --> 00:16:20.550
I will always be cheering for you wherever you are, as long as you're well and playing baseball.

00:16:30.740 --> 00:16:31.940
<i>Dad.</i>

00:16:32.350 --> 00:16:36.060
<i>Is it really okay if I go to America?</i>

00:16:38.490 --> 00:16:40.830
<i>After you died...</i>

00:16:40.830 --> 00:16:44.990
<i>Mom and Dad raised me like I was their own child.</i>

00:16:46.200 --> 00:16:48.410
<i>Me... who was always selfish.</i>

00:16:49.230 --> 00:16:54.000
<i>But am I going to leave that house because of my selfishness again?</i>

00:16:54.000 --> 00:16:56.510
<i>Upsetting them...</i>

00:17:01.340 --> 00:17:02.670
You're right.

00:17:02.670 --> 00:17:04.000
I understand, Dad.

00:17:04.000 --> 00:17:05.970
I should stay in Japan and-

00:17:05.200 --> 00:17:05.970
Goro.

00:17:08.710 --> 00:17:09.800
Dad!?

00:17:14.430 --> 00:17:16.510
U-Um, Dad...

00:17:16.510 --> 00:17:17.580
About going to America-

00:17:17.580 --> 00:17:20.580
I saw it and I know about Gibson's interview.

00:17:20.580 --> 00:17:21.570
Huh?

00:17:22.510 --> 00:17:26.450
If I talked to you about it, I knew you'd want to go.

00:17:26.450 --> 00:17:29.030
That's why I didn't say anything.

00:17:29.620 --> 00:17:32.510
I secretly contacted Katsuragi...

00:17:32.510 --> 00:17:34.990
and even asked them to get my number ready.

00:17:36.020 --> 00:17:38.580
I'm an unfair father.

00:17:38.980 --> 00:17:40.370
Dad...

00:17:42.600 --> 00:17:46.430
I was probably jealous of Honda somewhere.

00:17:47.120 --> 00:17:49.270
As a father.

00:17:51.300 --> 00:17:52.070
Goro.

00:17:53.500 --> 00:17:54.980
Go to America!

00:17:57.050 --> 00:18:02.440
If you're our son, fight it out on the best stage against the best men!

00:18:06.000 --> 00:18:06.740
Yeah.

00:18:11.550 --> 00:18:13.490
Sato-kun goes to the Warriors.

00:18:13.490 --> 00:18:15.100
And Mayumura-kun goes to the Oceans.

00:18:15.100 --> 00:18:16.870
You were both drafted as their first choice, huh?

00:18:17.370 --> 00:18:18.730
Congratulations.

00:18:18.730 --> 00:18:20.080
Thank you very much.

00:18:20.080 --> 00:18:24.050
Yakushiji-kun and Kusano-kun have also joined the professionals.

00:18:24.470 --> 00:18:25.340
Yes.

00:18:25.340 --> 00:18:27.010
I'm looking forward to fighting them in the professionals.

00:18:27.670 --> 00:18:29.010
You're right.

00:18:29.010 --> 00:18:31.970
And there's something else that I need to tell you.

00:18:33.310 --> 00:18:35.440
It's about the championship flag, right?

00:18:35.860 --> 00:18:37.110
Yes.

00:18:37.110 --> 00:18:42.770
After the board of directors investigated, Egashira finally admitted his actions.

00:18:42.770 --> 00:18:44.630
Even though it was his judgment, 

00:18:44.630 --> 00:18:50.360
as the baseball club, we have to take responsibility for injuring another school's student on purpose.

00:18:50.990 --> 00:18:56.230
It has been decided that we will inform the league and return the championship flag.

00:18:56.230 --> 00:19:01.830
This time it's our responsibility as executives for giving authority to Egashira.

00:19:02.980 --> 00:19:07.090
In the end, we've marred your win...

00:19:07.580 --> 00:19:09.330
We're really sorry.

00:19:09.330 --> 00:19:10.170
No.

00:19:10.170 --> 00:19:12.680
We're happy with the result.

00:19:13.270 --> 00:19:17.640
We've all talked it over and decided to fight for the championship flag in the professionals.

00:19:18.720 --> 00:19:20.630
We're looking forward to your progress.

00:19:21.570 --> 00:19:22.280
By the way,

00:19:22.280 --> 00:19:24.860
have you heard anything about Shigeno-kun?

00:19:25.230 --> 00:19:25.990
Oh.

00:19:25.990 --> 00:19:28.360
He told me himself.

00:19:28.830 --> 00:19:30.330
He's challenging the Majors!?

00:19:30.330 --> 00:19:31.390
Yeah.

00:19:31.390 --> 00:19:34.280
He ditched entering the pros and said he was going to go to tryouts.

00:19:34.280 --> 00:19:35.330
Geez.

00:19:35.330 --> 00:19:37.190
What is he thinking?

00:19:37.190 --> 00:19:39.380
Well, it does sound like Shigeno.

00:19:40.050 --> 00:19:43.030
He will always be a challenger.

00:19:43.740 --> 00:19:45.250
<i>What's he thinking?</i>

00:19:45.780 --> 00:19:48.490
<i>He's always acting cool.</i>

00:20:14.080 --> 00:20:14.950
Really!?

00:20:14.950 --> 00:20:16.750
Did I really pass!?

00:20:18.620 --> 00:20:19.860
Oh?

00:20:19.860 --> 00:20:21.440
So you really passed, Sis?

00:20:21.440 --> 00:20:22.630
What do you think!?

00:20:22.630 --> 00:20:25.830
This is the result of working hard for half the year without going out on a single date!

00:20:25.830 --> 00:20:27.510
You just don't have anyone to go out with, right?

00:20:27.510 --> 00:20:28.460
Oh yeah.

00:20:28.460 --> 00:20:30.420
I should let Honda know.

00:20:30.420 --> 00:20:33.180
Maybe I should get him to celebrate with me.

00:20:30.420 --> 00:20:32.090
Ignoring me, huh?

00:20:34.840 --> 00:20:35.780
What is it?

00:20:35.780 --> 00:20:37.130
Shouting so loud like that...

00:20:37.970 --> 00:20:39.300
Sorry, Sis...

00:20:39.300 --> 00:20:41.100
I totally forgot to tell you.

00:20:41.100 --> 00:20:46.100
Shigeno-senpai's plans were moved forward a week,
and he said that he was leaving for America today.

00:20:54.600 --> 00:20:57.280
So the first tryout is in Arizona, huh?

00:20:57.880 --> 00:21:00.500
Well, just go out there and give it all you got.

00:21:00.500 --> 00:21:01.900
Be careful, okay?

00:21:01.900 --> 00:21:04.750
Call home whenever you feel lonely.

00:21:06.190 --> 00:21:08.340
You really think I'd get homesick?

00:21:09.180 --> 00:21:10.600
I'm joking! I'm joking!

00:21:10.600 --> 00:21:12.140
I'll call to say I love you every day!

00:21:13.130 --> 00:21:14.810
Passengers for Los Angeles.

00:21:14.810 --> 00:21:20.340
Flight 7871. Please make your way to gate 18.

00:21:15.980 --> 00:21:19.010
Then I'll be on my way.

00:21:19.440 --> 00:21:20.340
Yeah.

00:21:22.810 --> 00:21:24.310
Honda!

00:21:28.890 --> 00:21:30.480
Shimizu?

00:21:30.480 --> 00:21:31.340
Hey!

00:21:31.340 --> 00:21:32.940
The curry lady!

00:21:33.500 --> 00:21:34.220
T-Thank God.

00:21:34.220 --> 00:21:35.750
T-Thank God.

00:21:35.750 --> 00:21:37.770
I thought I wasn't going to make it.

00:21:38.890 --> 00:21:42.660
Did you come all this way just to see me off?

00:21:43.290 --> 00:21:44.430
That's right.

00:21:44.430 --> 00:21:45.630
You have a problem with that?

00:21:46.340 --> 00:21:47.620
It's because...

00:21:48.030 --> 00:21:53.590
It's because someone is going to disappear from me again.

00:21:59.010 --> 00:22:00.230
Lift... your head.

00:22:00.230 --> 00:22:01.470
Lift... your head.

00:22:02.040 --> 00:22:04.600
I have to go now.

00:22:04.600 --> 00:22:08.520
At least let me see your smile one last time.

00:22:19.260 --> 00:22:20.380
Do your best, okay?

00:22:20.380 --> 00:22:24.370
I won't forgive you if you forget your promise to me about your first autograph, okay?

00:22:25.640 --> 00:22:26.640
Yeah.

00:24:41.460 --> 00:24:44.290
I've finally come this far, Dad.

00:24:44.290 --> 00:24:48.700
I'm just going to go attack the homeland of the man that's waiting for me.

00:24:48.700 --> 00:24:49.600
Bye, Japan.

00:24:50.420 --> 00:24:55.520
Whatever sky we're under, as long as we're playing baseball, we're one!

00:24:56.120 --> 00:24:58.730
Watch my battle!
